  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Applying the Human Security Approach to Advance an Integrated Response to Health and Migration in the Northern Triangle of Central America and Mexico</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The design of the programme is rooted in the complex and interconnected challenges present in El Salvador, Guatemala, Honduras, and Mexico, proposing a three-phased implementation process to achieve its overall programme goal of accelerate progress toward improving migrants&#x2019; access to comprehensive, quality health services, with equity and non-discrimination, in the Northern Triangle of Central America and Mexico, through enhancing  national and community-centered multi-stakeholder coordination on health and migration; strengthening health information systems to support migrant-inclusive policies and programmes; and building the capacity of governmental and non-governmental actors on the added value of the human security approach for  promoting a people-centered, participatory  and development response to health and migration. For this purpose, PAHO/WHO and IOM will establish a Joint Programme Team to convene personnel with technical expertise to support and provide guidance on activities during all phases.</narrative>
  </description>
